			'isiZulu. In Census 2022 it was the language most often spoken in the household for 24.4% of the population (up from 22.8% in 1996), ahead of isiXhosa (16.3%) and Afrikaans (10.6%). In KwaZulu-Natal, 80.0% of people speak isiZulu at home.',
